-5.6399 50.3134,-5.7621 50.2817,-5.8908 50.2519,-6.0218 50.2235,-6.1512 50.1958,-6.2748 50.1681,-6.3888 50.1398,-6.4889 50.1103,-6.5713 50.0789,-6.6319 50.0449,-6.6666 50.0252,-6.6755 50.0047,-6.6803 49.9835,-6.6813"]}],"category":["Met"],"certainty":"Likely","description":"Showers, heavy and thundery, will reach southwest England and Wales later Sunday morning, before spreading and developing more widely during the afternoon. Whilst some areas will miss the heaviest showers, where they do occur 10-15 mm of rain is possible in less than an hour, with 30-40 mm possible over several hours, these larger totals most likely for parts of north and northwest England and southwest Scotland. Hail, frequent lightning and, in southern parts of England and Wales, wind gusts of 35-45 mph will be additional hazards. Heaviest showers and thunderstorms will become more isolated later in the evening.\n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","event":"Yellow thunderstorm warning","expires":"2026-08-30T22:59:00+00:00","headline":"Heavy showers and thunderstorms bringing disruption to transport, infrastructure and outdoor activities.","instruction":"Give yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, or bus and train timetables, amending your travel plans if necessary.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nConsider if your location is at risk of flash flooding. If so, consider preparing a flood plan and an emergency flood kit.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","language":"en-GB","onset":"2026-08-30T10:00:00+00:00","parameter":[{"value":"2; Yellow; Moderate","valueName":"awareness_level"},{"value":"3; Thunderstorm","valueName":"awareness_type"},{"value":"There is a good chance driving conditions will be affected by spray, standing water and/or hail, leading to longer journey times by car and bus","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Delays to train services are possible","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Probably some damage to a few buildings and structures from lightning strikes","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Some short-term loss of power and other services is likely","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Some flooding of a few homes and businesses possible, leading to some damage to buildings or structures","valueName":"impacts"}],"responseType":["Prepare"],"senderName":"UK Met Office","severity":"Moderate","urgency":"Future","web":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings"}],"msgType":"Alert","scope":"Public","sender":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","sent":"2026-08-30T07:47:53+00:00","source":"2.49.0.0.826.0.GB","status":"Actual"},"raw_properties":{"supersededByAlertId":null,"supersededAt":null,"supersedeType":null,"geometryDescription":"geometry is bbox only, link (member of the feature's links array) with type application/geo+json points to geojson describing the exact shape","geometryType":"bbox","OBJECTID":"7db66de8-4545-4e87-b21b-307721563429","alertId":"7fc4f40e-adf0-4002-b2ae-aab2fe763cef","countryCode":"UK","featureType":"polygon","hubLanguage":"en-GB","indexArea":0,"indexFeature":0,"indexInfo":0,"hubTime":"2026-08-30T07:48:44Z","hubLink":"https://meteo.fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com/api/archive/warnings/7fc4f40e-adf0-4002-b2ae-aab2fe763cef.xml?AWSAccessKeyId=DO00LYPLJBWUUWC6D6NU&Expires=1788128715&Signature=eRVjI8S5bM6AgJc%2FQX%2BLhCV1